1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:05,060
Welcome to MatchPulse Live, hosted on
Azure Container Apps. This fictional match

2
00:00:05,060 --> 00:00:09,740
follows Northbridge City and Harbor United
through synthetic football events.

3
00:00:10,160 --> 00:00:14,160
The analysis uses accepted events, not a
live feed.

4
00:00:17,920 --> 00:00:21,360
Each match moment links to the event the
system accepted.

5
00:00:21,680 --> 00:00:26,400
You can trace the source behind an insight
and inspect its supporting evidence.

6
00:00:27,920 --> 00:00:31,760
After a synthetic goal event is accepted,
Northbridge City’s

7
00:00:31,760 --> 00:00:36,240
score increases. The event stays linked to
its resulting insight.

8
00:00:37,980 --> 00:00:42,160
Replaying the same event does not add
another goal or change the score.

9
00:00:42,480 --> 00:00:47,260
Out-of-order events are rejected, so
accepted match state stays consistent.

10
00:00:53,920 --> 00:00:57,700
Fan view puts the verified moment first in
a clear summary.

11
00:00:58,340 --> 00:01:01,060
Accepted event evidence keeps it in
context.

12
00:01:02,940 --> 00:01:07,840
Analyst view shows the calculation,
inputs, and evidence identifiers,

13
00:01:08,160 --> 00:01:12,220
so you can trace how an insight was
formed. Broadcaster view

14
00:01:12,220 --> 00:01:16,460
condenses that same insight and match
facts for a live overlay.

15
00:01:19,920 --> 00:01:21,420
English, Spanish, and French

16
00:01:21,420 --> 00:01:25,280
versions change the wording but preserve
the same match evidence.

17
00:01:27,020 --> 00:01:30,380
Northbridge City beats Harbor United two
goals to one.

18
00:01:30,520 --> 00:01:35,140
The recap connects the score to accepted
match events, not outside data.

19
00:01:38,920 --> 00:01:41,660
This deployment uses deterministic
fallback.

20
00:01:41,820 --> 00:01:45,260
Foundry is disabled, with zero model calls
in the demo.

21
00:01:47,920 --> 00:01:49,840
This demo uses synthetic data,

22
00:01:49,920 --> 00:01:53,150
not a live feed. Both teams and the match
are fictional.
